This is a complete guide to building a full-stack application using **React**, **Node.js**, and **Express.js**.

We will build a simple **"User Management System"** where you can:
1.  Create a user (Add dummy data).
2.  View a list of users.
3.  Delete a user.

---

### Part 1: Project Setup

First, create a main folder for your project and set up the folder structure.

```bash
mkdir my-fullstack-app
cd my-fullstack-app
```

---

### Part 2: Backend (Node.js + Express)

1.  **Initialize the backend:**
    ```bash
    mkdir backend
    cd backend
    npm init -y
    npm install express cors nodemon
    ```

2.  **Create the server file (`index.js`):**
    Create a file named `index.js` inside the `backend` folder.

    ```javascript
    // backend/index.js
    const express = require('express');
    const cors = require('cors');
    const app = express();
    const PORT = 5000;

    // Middleware
    app.use(cors()); // Allows React to talk to Express
    app.use(express.json());

    // Dummy Data
    let users = [
      { id: 1, name: 'Alice Johnson', email: 'alice@example.com' },
      { id: 2, name: 'Bob Smith', email: 'bob@example.com' },
      { id: 3, name: 'Charlie Brown', email: 'charlie@example.com' }
    ];

    // --- API Routes ---

    // 1. Get All Users
    app.get('/api/users', (req, res) => {
      res.json(users);
    });

    // 2. Add New User
    app.post('/api/users', (req, res) => {
      const { name, email } = req.body;
      const newUser = { id: users.length + 1, name, email };
      users.push(newUser);
      res.status(201).json(newUser);
    });

    // 3. Delete User
    app.delete('/api/users/:id', (req, res) => {
      const id = parseInt(req.params.id);
      users = users.filter(user => user.id !== id);
      res.status(200).json({ message: 'User deleted' });
    });

    // Start Server
    app.listen(PORT, () => {
      console.log(`Server is running on http://localhost:${PORT}`);
    });
    ```

3.  **Update `package.json` scripts:**
    In `backend/package.json`, add this to the `"scripts"` section:
    ```json
    "start": "nodemon index.js"
    ```

